# 16. Search should remain boring

Do not install Elasticsearch because "search system."

Start:

```text
Postgres FTS
+
pg_trgm
```

Then a secondary semantic retrieval system:

```text
embedding(passages)
```

But maintain:

[
\text{vector similarity} \neq \text{knowledge relation}
]

Embeddings help discover.

They do not alter canonical graph truth.

If search eventually becomes measurably hot:

```text
Rust + Tantivy
```

becomes attractive.

Exactly as the performance docs recommend.

