# 17. DuckDB + Parquet are massively useful here

Your canonical mutable state remains Postgres.

But compiling/analyzing huge scholarly datasets is a different workload.

For:

```text
10 million passages
all evidence edges
benchmark analysis
bulk graph transformations
translation statistics
```

write Parquet.

Then DuckDB can query it efficiently offline.

Conceptually:

```text
POSTGRES
live truth

R2
immutable objects

PARQUET
bulk analytical truth snapshot
```

Don't make Postgres serve every analytical job.

And don't make JSONL your analytics format.

`SPEC-00` explicitly recommends Parquet + Zstd for serious bulk publication.

