# 27. The final formal Pāṭala model

I would now make these three planes explicit in every architecture document:

```text
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                TRUTH PLANE                   │
│                                              │
│ objects / evidence / events / authority      │
│ PostgreSQL + Pāṭala Kernel                   │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                      │
                      ▼
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│               COMPILE PLANE                  │
│                                              │
│ dependencies / hashes / staleness / tasks    │
│ Python + Hermes + DuckDB + optional Rust     │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                      │
                      ▼
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                 READ PLANE                   │
│                                              │
│ immutable HTML / JSON / bundles / Parquet    │
│ R2 + Cloudflare CDN + thin Workers/MCP       │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

And one governing law for each:

```text
TRUTH PLANE
Nothing becomes true because an agent says so.

COMPILE PLANE
Nothing recomputes unless its dependencies changed.

